# XSH at_quick_exit()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Each test forks a child that registers handlers and ends with
# quick_exit(); handlers report with write() on a pipe and the parent judges.

assertion  XSH.at_quick_exit.001
anchor     functions/at_quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/at_quick_exit.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       at_quick_exit() of a function returns 0, and quick_exit() then
           calls that function once, with no argument.
test       t/001-registers.c

assertion  XSH.at_quick_exit.002
anchor     functions/at_quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/at_quick_exit.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       At least 32 registrations are possible: 32 registrations (of one
           function) all return 0 and quick_exit() makes all 32 calls.
test       t/002-thirty-two.c

assertion  XSH.at_quick_exit.003
anchor     functions/at_quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/at_quick_exit.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       A registration that returned 0 is honoured and none that returned
           non-zero is: after up to 4096 registrations of one function,
           quick_exit() calls it exactly as many times as registrations
           succeeded.
note       Registering past the limit may succeed or fail; both are accepted.
test       t/003-count-matches.c
